            <ArticleTitle>Pseudoxanthoma elasticum with dipyridamole-induced coronary artery spasm: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>806-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In patients with pseudoxanthoma elasticum, severe organic coronary artery stenosis often occurs without coronary risk factors. However, this report presents the case of a 49-year-old woman with pseudoxanthoma elasticum who had coronary artery spasm with an angiographically normal coronary artery. In addition, coronary artery spasm was provoked with dipyridamole thallium-201 cardiac imaging.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
